 ## Background
-Spherical Harmonics are a set of orthogonal functions defined on the sphere, commonly used in computer graphics to represent lighting and reflectance. The specific hardcoded polynomial evaluation method is popularized by the original 3D Gaussian Splatting implementation and its various forks [S1, S2, S3, unofficial].
